    "disable_comparison": "true",
    "angles": "- About 17,000 new and they trade near that or above it today -- this one has not depreciated like a normal Audi. Never say it lost value.\n- Americans waited eighteen years for this. Audi sold the RS6 as a wagon in Europe for three generations and sent none of them here -- the C6 and C7 Avants were never imported at all.\n- The last RS6 sold in America was a 2003 sedan, not a wagon. 860 of them, one model year, and then nothing until 2021.\n- 591 horsepower and 590 lb-ft from a 4.0-litre twin-turbo V8, zero to sixty in about 3.6 seconds.\n- A wagon that outruns the sports car its own badge sits on, and still swallows a dog crate and a set of wheels.",
