  "script": "They trade for about $130,000 today\u2014 this one that hasn't really depreciated. The RS6 Avant finally came to the U.S. in 2020, after eighteen years of European exclusivity. Its 4.0-liter twin-turbo V8 delivers 591 horsepower and 590 lb-ft of torque. This engine doesn't have a redline listed, but it roars. Power flows through an eight-speed automatic and Audi\u2019s Quattro AWD system, making it a beast in all seasons. Inside, it blends sporty design with practicality, featuring leather and a Bang & Olufsen sound system. You\u2019ll find it\u2019s got room for the whole family. Outrunning many sports cars, it has a 0-60 time of just 3.6 seconds, impressive for a wagon. Its rivals struggle to match this performance in a wagon form. So, would you choose a wagon that keeps its value, or go for something with a sportier badge?",
